title: The Rentenmark
subtitle: The inflation ends, and the bill is presented to the workers.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month = 12 and e23_rentenmark_done = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
Q.e23_rentenmark_done = 1;
Q.inflation = 12;
Q.stability += 12;
if (Q.e22_workers_gov == 0) {
    Q.chancellor = 'Wilhelm Marx';
    Q.government_name = 'Marx cabinet (Centre, DDP, DVP, BVP)';
    Q.spd_in_government = 0; Q.zentrum_in_government = 1; Q.ddp_in_government = 1; Q.dvp_in_government = 1; Q.bvp_in_government = 1;
}
!}

= The Rentenmark

On 15 November the new Rentenmark went into circulation, one to a trillion old marks, backed on paper by a mortgage on all German land. Hjalmar Schacht stopped the presses. To everyone's surprise, it holds. By December a loaf of bread costs the same in the evening as in the morning.

[? if e22_workers_gov = 0 : Stresemann lost a vote of confidence on 23 November, and Wilhelm Marx of the Centre now governs without the SPD. ?] The price of stability is paid in the works. Hundreds of thousands of officials are dismissed. The unemployed number in the millions. A decree allows the employers to lengthen the working day, and the eight-hour day, the last gain of November 1918, is gone in all but name.

The workers who joined the party in the year of hunger are tired. Some are leaving.

- @hours: Fight for the eight-hour day in every works.
- @unemployed: Organise the unemployed.
- @consolidate: Consolidate: train the new members, close the gaps.

@hours
subtitle: [? if lock_union_work = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The unions are broke, but the issue is everyone's.
choose-if: lock_union_work < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids work inside the reformist unions.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_union_work == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.worker_support += 4;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

Our factory cells lead a hundred small strikes for the eight-hour day. Most are lost. The workers remember who led them.

@unemployed
subtitle: The Left's answer. A new base among the desperate.
on-arrival: {!
Q.militancy += 4;
Q.worker_support += 2;
Q.district_berlin_members *= 1.04;
Q.district_ruhr_members *= 1.04;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

Committees of the unemployed meet at the labour exchanges in Berlin and the Ruhr. Their marches will become a feature of German winters.

@consolidate
subtitle: The Spartacist answer. Fewer members leave.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity += 6;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    Q['district_' + d + '_loyalty'] += 3;
}
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

The party schools reopen in back rooms. The new members learn their Marx, and the old ones learn patience.
